# docker/.dockerignore — the build-context filter for the node image.
# The build context is the CLONE ROOT (`plugins-src/dsh-meta-community`), because the Dockerfile copies `src/` and `docker/snapshots/` from it.
# Measured why this file matters: the clone root is 51,784,008 B in 618 files (census 2026-10-19, `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -File -Force | Measure-Object Length -Sum`) and 51,542,113 B of that in 591 files (99.53%) is `node_modules`, none of which the image consumes — the node runs from source under Node 24 type stripping, so there is no npm install and no bundler step to feed.
# Docker resolves its ignore file by the DOCKERFILE's path, not by an arbitrary file named `.dockerignore`: with `-f docker/Dockerfile` the effective file is `docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, and a context-root `.dockerignore` is the fallback. This file is the artifact of record named by the NODE-CONTRACT; `docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore` is the same rule set under the name Docker actually reads, and the two are kept byte-identical (verified in the build report) so they cannot drift.
node_modules
**/node_modules
lib
**/lib
*.log
**/*.log
.git
.gitignore
pnpm-lock.yaml
tsconfig.json
tsdown.config.ts
cordis.patch.yml
CHARTER.md
README.md
coverage
